16389144,2025-10-06,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I recently obtained my credit report and found information that is inaccurate and harmful to my credit history. Specifically, my credit file contains an account ( XXXX, Account Number XXXX XXXXXXXX ) that I never authorized to be reported, nor did I give my consent for it to be furnished to any credit reporting agency. 
At no time did I provide written authorization, verifiable electronic consent, or any other form of permission allowing this information to be included in my credit file. 

LEGAL VIOLATIONS : FCRA Section 604 ( 15 U.S.C. 1681b ) Lack of permissible purpose. 
A consumers credit file may only contain information obtained for a permissible purpose, which generally requires the consumers express consent. The inclusion of this account and the related inquiries in my filewithout documented proof of my consentconstitutes a direct violation of this section and represents the unauthorized use and disclosure of my non-public personal information. 

FCRA Section 605B ( 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ) Blocking disputed information. 
When a consumer submits a report to the Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ) or local law enforcement identifying disputed items, the credit reporting agency must block that information within XXXX ( XXXX ) business days. I submitted such a report ( Police Report Case XXXX XXXXXXXX ), which clearly identifies the disputed items. Despite this, TransUnion continues to report the account and the inquiries, causing ongoing harm. 

FCRA Section 607 ( b ) ( 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) ) Maximum possible accuracy. 
TransUnion has failed to maintain only accurate, verifiable, and complete information. The lack of verifiable documentation from the furnisher or the agency demonstrates that this legal standard has not been met. 

PERSONAL IMPACT : I have been denied for legitimate credit applications due to this unauthorized account. 

When approved for credit, I am forced to pay significantly higher interest rates. 

I was recently denied rental housing because of this negative information. 

My insurance premiums are higher due to credit-based pricing. 

