LEGAL VIOLATIONS : FCRA Section 604 ( 15 U.S.C. 1681b ) Lack of Permissible Purpose A consumers credit file may only contain information obtained for a permissible purpose, which generally requires the consumers express consent. The inclusion of this account and the related inquiries in my filewithout documented proof of my consentconstitutes a direct violation of this section and represents the unauthorized use and disclosure of my non-public personal information. 

FCRA Section 605B ( 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ) Blocking Disputed Information When a consumer submits a valid identity theft or police report identifying disputed items, the credit reporting agency must block that information within four ( 4 ) business days. I submitted such documentation through my Police Report ( Case No. XXXX ), which clearly identifies the disputed account. Despite this, Equifax continues to report the account and related inquiries, causing ongoing harm.

FCRA Section 607 ( b ) ( 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) ) Maximum Possible Accuracy Equifax has failed to maintain only accurate, verifiable, and complete information. The lack of verifiable documentation from the furnisher or the agency demonstrates that this legal standard has not been met. Reporting an account that lacks any proof of authorization violates the CRAs duty to ensure maximum possible accuracy.

PERSONAL IMPACT : I have been denied for legitimate credit applications due to this unauthorized account. 

When approved for credit, I am forced to pay significantly higher interest rates. 

I was recently denied rental housing because of this negative information. 

My insurance premiums are higher due to credit-based pricing. 

