TransUnion did not handle my dispute as required. Instead of opening a separate investigation, they merged my mailed dispute into an online dispute submitted XX/XX/XXXX that was unrelated, then posted the results online. They never sent me written results even though I specifically requested them. 

Under FCRA 1681i ( a ) ( 6 ) ( A ) ( B ), TransUnion must provide written notice of reinvestigation results within five business days of completion, and under 1681i ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ) each dispute must receive its own reinvestigation. I did not consent to electronic delivery or merging of disputes. TransUnions actions denied me a fair reinvestigation and proper written notice as required by law.

Failure to Correct Inaccurate Reporting TransUnion continues to report this timeshare as 120+ days late each month, even though XXXX  and XXXX  deleted the same account from my credit report in XXXX after determining that the information was inaccurate or unverifiable. This shows that the other nationwide credit bureaus found the data invalid, yet TransUnion refuses to correct it. The account has had no activity or payments since XX/XX/XXXX and should be aged from that original delinquency date. By continuing to refresh the late status, TransUnion is re-aging the account in violation of FCRA 1681c ( a ) ( 4 ) and 623 ( a ) ( 5 ), extending the reporting period beyond seven years.

FCRA Violations TransUnions conduct violates multiple provisions of the FCRA, including : 1681i ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ) failure to conduct a reasonable reinvestigation 1681i ( a ) ( 6 ) ( A ) ( B ) failure to provide written notice of results 1681e ( b ) failure to maintain reasonable procedures for accuracy 1681c ( a ) ( 4 ) reporting adverse information beyond seven years 1681s-2 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ) furnishing information known to be inaccurate or misleading Requested Action I request that the CFPB investigate TransUnions actions and require the following : ( 1 ) Deletion of the ASNY Company tradeline from my TransUnion credit report.

( 2 ) Written notice of reinvestigation results as required by 1681i ( a ) ( 6 ). 
( 3 ) Confirmation that TransUnion will cease merging unrelated disputes and will ensure consumers receive written results when requested.

Harm Caused TransUnions inaccurate and procedurally improper reporting has caused ongoing harm by lowering my credit score, preventing me from obtaining credit on fair terms, and denying me my statutory right to a proper reinvestigation. 

