16621450,2025-10-17,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau Representative, I am filing this formal complaint against Regional Acceptance Corporation for the continued and unlawful reporting of a derogatory auto loan account across the consumer reporting agencies XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX 

This account is listed as Charged Off and Paid in Full/WAS A CHARGE OFF, with closure and last activity dates around 2019, per my TransUnion report ( Account XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  ). Despite being paid in full, this account is still being reported as a charge-off and remains marked as adverse, which is false, inaccurate, and misleading. 

1. Violations of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) According to 15 U.S.C. 1681a and 1681b, no information should appear on a consumers report without their written authorization or a permissible purpose. I never authorized the inclusion of adverse or post-closure remarks once the account was paid and closed. Continued reporting after resolution constitutes unauthorized use of my consumer information.

Further, under 15 U.S.C. 1681c, consumer reporting agencies are prohibited from including any adverse item older than seven years, and only criminal convictions may lawfully remain longer. This account, closed since 2019, is now within the time frame for mandatory removal, especially since it was marked Paid in Full. 

Additionally, the accounts simultaneous reporting as both charge-off and paid is a direct violation of the accuracy and fairness requirements under 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ), which mandates that consumer reporting agencies adopt reasonable procedures to ensure maximum possible accuracy.

2. False Representation and Defamation of Credit Character Labeling a paid account as Charge-Off implies a loss to the creditor, not a consumer payment in full. This reporting damages my creditworthiness and misrepresents the true state of the account, thereby violating my right to fair and accurate reporting as required by 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( Dispute process ) and 1681s-2 ( a ) ( Duties of furnishers to provide accurate information ).

3. Unlawful Retention of Obsolete Data Under 15 U.S.C. 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ), any adverse information older than seven years must be excluded from reports. Since this account was closed and paid in 2019, the continued reporting until 2026as stated by XXXX unlawful and must be immediately deleted. 

4. Identity Misuse and Unauthorized Re-reporting Per 12 CFR 1022.3 and 15 U.S.C. 1681c2, any information added to my report without written consent can be treated as identity theft or unauthorized use of my data. Reporting a paid and closed account as a continuing derogatory charge-off qualifies as such unauthorized behavior.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,TRUIST FINANCIAL CORPORATION,TX,76036,,Web,2025-10-17,Closed with explanation,Yes
