My dispute was filed in compliance with all procedural requirements, yet Equifax took longer than 30 days to respond, directly violating federal law.

This unlawful delaycombined with their continued publication of inaccurate and damaging informationconstitutes a clear and deliberate disregard for consumer rights and has materially harmed my creditworthiness.

Equifax received my dispute identifying multiple inaccurate, unverifiable, and misleading accounts that are being reported under my name.

Despite having the full legal timeframe to investigate and correct these errors, Equifax : Failed to provide results within 30 days, as mandated by FCRA.

Continued to report derogatory data after the legal period expired.

Failed to verify the accounts with the original furnishers, violating both procedural accuracy and timeliness requirements.

