tand what the person was saying because of their aggravated tone and accent. I was asking nicely for them to repeat it but they were getting very frustrated with me and raising their voice. They also accused me of not listening to what they were saying, but I just could not understand because they were speaking fast in their accent and not using proper XXXX grammar. I never raised my voice at them, and I felt like I was not receiving adequate customer service. I composed an email appealing the decision they made on XX/XX/year>. I waited to hear back from them, but received nothing. I thought this was extremely unprofessional considering I had got {$500.00} stolen from me, which I tried to stress the urgency of the situation to them. I was out of the country at the time, and needed money to be able to get home. Money I had set aside to get home was now going to have to be put towards a charge that I did not make. Finally, when I returned back to the country on XX/XX/year> I called the credit card company to see what else I could do. Again, the person talking to me was not being kind even though I was remaining completely calm. They informed me that my appeal was rejected yet I never got an email or a call back from them to let me know that. I tried to ask why they rejected my appeal and they said the same thing about it being tracked back to me. I tried to express to them I believe my identity and information had been stolen because thats why it was tracked back to me. I also asked them if I could cancel the credit card because somebody had my information and could continue to charge me. They rejected this and said I couldnt cancel unless I paid the balance off of the card. I denied to pay the balance because I was not going to pay off a fraudulent charge. The customer service agent accused me of lying and saying that I made that purchase. I tried to ask them how they knew I made the purchase and what the address was that this supposed item was sent to. They would no