16789821,2025-10-24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"BACKGROUND AND FORMAL DEMAND This correspondence constitutes my formal I6B3 compliance and evidentiary audit trail demand regarding the continued reporting of the above-referenced XXXX XXXX XXXX account on my XXXX XXXX consumer report XXXX The data remains verified as accurate despite the absence of any legally sufficient verification materials, constituting willful and negligent non-compliance under 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ( Reinvestigation of Disputed Information ) and 1681s-2 ( b ) ( Duties of Furnishers ). 

Pursuant to the controlling federal law and related CFPB regulations, I now require full evidentiary disclosure and deletion compliance under the following provisions : 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ( 5 ) ( A ) ( i ) ( ii ) Requires deletion of unverifiable data.

15 U.S.C. 1681b Limits permissible purpose for continued dissemination of unverifiable data.

12 C.F.R. 1000.6.34 ( c ) Mandates fair and transparent data handling by consumer reporting entities.

I6B3 XXXX XXXX Code ( FCRA Section 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ) ) Requires deletion when reinvestigation fails to verify with primary-source evidence.

