XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX 

Transmission IDs and system routing confirmations showing when Experian transmitted and received dispute data. 

Internal Case Handling Logs : The full name, employee ID, title, and department of each Experian employee or contractor who reviewed, verified, or closed my reinvestigation.

Copies of any internal verified/accurate case notes, comments, or system auto-response entries.

Furnisher Verification Records : The name, title/department, and employee identification number of any XXXX XXXX personnel who allegedly verified the accounts accuracy.

Copies of the original primary-source evidence they relied upon ( not screenshots, summaries, or billing extracts ). 

Furnishers transmission confirmation from their compliance system, showing the exact date/time of verified status return to Clarity Services XXXX 

Prohibition & Confirmation of Evidence Use : A written certification confirming that Experian did not rely solely on account statements, screenshots, payment history reproductions, or any derivative images as the basis for validation, consistent with 12 C.F.R. 1000.6.34 ( c ) and CFPB validation guidance. 

Identification of whether any automated matching algorithms were used during reinvestigation, including threshold criteria for verification. 

Deletion Compliance ( I6B3 ) : Confirm that Clarity Services has implemented FCRA 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ) protocols ( I6B3 ) and that unverifiable items are automatically deleted when primary evidence is not supplied by the furnisher within the prescribed reinvestigation window. 

III. LEGAL PRECEDENT SUPPORTING DELETION DEMAND The following precedents directly govern this dispute and compel deletion when verification is unsupported by primary-source evidence : XXXX XXXX Equifax, XXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXX XXXX. XXXX ) : Consumer Reporting Agencies must delete information that can not be verified through direct, documented evidence. Failure to do so violates 1681i. 

XXXX v. TransUnion, XXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXX XXXX. XXXX ) : Reinserted or re-verified data must meet CRAs accuracy obligations, and verification requires more than perfunctory reliance on the furnishers database. 

